<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35134" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perjūrus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		per-jus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>who breaks his
			oath</i>, <i>perjured</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid inter perjurum et mendacem?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rosc. Com. 16, 46</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perjurissimus leno,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 7, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perjura Troja,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 5, 811</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perjuri arte Sinonis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 195</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perjuras puellas punire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					3, 8, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perjura fides,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 24, 59</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Juv. 13, 174</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in gen., <i>who lies
				under oath</i>, <i>false</i>, <i>lying</i> (Plautin.), <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil.
				4, 2, 74</span></i>. —<i>Comp.</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil.
				1, 1, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Trin. 1, 2, 164</span></i>.—<i>Sup.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perjurissime hominum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 1, 3, 117</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Rud. 5, 3, 19</span></i>.</div>
